1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,506
A customer can send a token.

2
00:00:02,726 --> 00:00:05,435
A merchant still needs to know which order was paid.

3
00:00:05,655 --> 00:00:09,709
RelayGuard connects those two things, using MUSD on Mezo.

4
00:00:10,279 --> 00:00:11,879
Here's the merchant workspace.

5
00:00:12,099 --> 00:00:18,371
Connect an account, verify a receiving wallet, and create an invoice with an exact price and expiry.

6
00:00:18,591 --> 00:00:20,596
Funds go directly to the merchant.

7
00:00:21,166 --> 00:00:23,939
The customer opens the payment link on their phone.

8
00:00:24,159 --> 00:00:28,362
They see the amount, destination, and network before connecting a wallet.

9
00:00:28,582 --> 00:00:30,737
An ownership signature starts checkout.

10
00:00:30,957 --> 00:00:33,773
A separate wallet confirmation sends the payment.

11
00:00:34,343 --> 00:00:36,327
A transaction hash isn't enough.

12
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:43,224
RelayGuard checks the receipt and the matching MUSD transfer: the payer, recipient, and exact amount.

13
00:00:43,444 --> 00:00:45,791
Only then can the invoice become paid.

14
00:00:46,011 --> 00:00:50,384
Historical Testnet payments can be inspected in the public evidence panel.

15
00:00:50,954 --> 00:00:53,045
For developers, there's a second path.

16
00:00:53,265 --> 00:00:57,425
Register an API route and its price, then use the Express adapter.

17
00:00:57,645 --> 00:01:01,783
An unpaid request receives an HTTP 402 challenge.

18
00:01:02,003 --> 00:01:08,809
The facilitator settles the signed MUSD authorization before the API releases its response.

19
00:01:09,379 --> 00:01:11,896
Mezo also informs treasury decisions.

20
00:01:12,116 --> 00:01:15,636
These controlled scenarios run the real policy functions.

21
00:01:15,856 --> 00:01:20,016
At 125 percent collateral, human approval is required.

22
00:01:20,236 --> 00:01:23,116
Below 110 percent, spending is blocked.

23
00:01:23,336 --> 00:01:27,261
If protocol reads fail, MUSD authorization pauses.

24
00:01:27,831 --> 00:01:33,293
The public reviewer lets anyone inspect those boundaries and receipt evidence without a wallet.

25
00:01:33,513 --> 00:01:36,137
That makes the integration easier to verify.

26
00:01:36,707 --> 00:01:41,123
Our first users are MUSD API sellers and digital merchants.

27
00:01:41,343 --> 00:01:47,892
The next milestone is three design partners, measuring time to first payment, completion, and repeat use.

28
00:01:48,112 --> 00:01:54,640
RelayGuard gives sellers a practical way to accept MUSD, with payment evidence they can inspect.
